course: dictionary
lesson: 7374
title: Plod and slow words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a word's meaning from the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «Squeeze a clump of wet moss into a dish and you may see water bears, tiny tardigrades plodding about like chubby bears in slow motion.» Slow motion is the clue. Plodding means moving slowly.
explain: «In the film Ice Age, Manny the mammoth plods through the snow in shaggy fur.» Snow and a great shaggy animal are clues that something heavy is moving slowly and with effort. So plod means to walk slowly and heavily.
explain: Plod can also mean working slowly and steadily. "Plod on with homework" means keep going, even when the task is boring or hard. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Plod» means to walk slowly and heavily, as if tired.
fact: «Plod» can also mean to work slowly and steadily at something boring or hard.
fact: A «plod» is a slow, heavy walk.
fact: In UK slang, «the plod» means the police. It is a bit cheeky and mocking, not polite.
exercise: «Manny the mammoth plods through the snow in shaggy fur.» What does plods mean here? | *Walks slowly and heavily | Jumps over the snow | Runs quickly and lightly | Sits down and sleeps
exercise: Mum says, "Plod on with your homework." What does she want you to do? | Forget about it until tomorrow | Finish it all in one second | *Keep working slowly and steadily | Throw your homework away
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means moving slowly: «Water bears, tiny tardigrades, plodding about like chubby bears in slow motion.» | water | chubby | *plodding | motion
test: «After the long hike, we plodded back to the campsite through the mud.» What does plodded mean? | Raced home | Sang a song | *Walked slowly and tiredly | Danced happily
test: A character says, "The plod are coming!" In UK slang, who are they? | Shopkeepers | Pigs | *The police | Doctors
exam: Which sentence uses plod to mean working steadily at something boring? | *"I will plod on with my spellings until they are done." | "We laughed at the funny film." | "The lion pounced on its prey." | "The stars shone brightly tonight."
